    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "01\nSTATED\nMake composition mandatory\n\nConsumers require policy sections instead of optional operational numbers and local defaults. Code stays in the CLI package; the policy packag",
      "href": "#decision-contract",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "02\nSTATED\nUse one set of byte capacities\n\nCapture, spool, file decoding, worker validation and socket framing receive policy-backed caps. Chunk, inline, per-result and aggregate li",
      "href": "#decision-output",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "03\nSTATED\nRead the derived memory limits\n\nThe app’s duplicate memory-policy class and reconstruction disappear. RSS thresholds, worker heap limit, sampling cadence and replacement ",
      "href": "#decision-resources",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "04\nSTATED\nKeep distinct clocks and retention limits\n\nStartup, shutdown, idle life, acknowledgement waiting, log rotation/queueing and trace retention take their own policy fields. ",
      "href": "#decision-clocks",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "05\nSTATED\nChoose the timeout by caller purpose\n\nSocket inactivity timers use 100 ms for status observation and 250 ms for ordinary lifecycle / execution-status. Execute admission u",
      "href": "#decision-deadlines",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "06\nSTATED\nPut numbers on existing retry scopes\n\nStartup child retries and accepted-execute reattachments become numeric loops. Fetch resume has a per-execute counter. Defaults are ",
      "href": "#decision-attempts",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "07\nUNEXPLAINED\nLet a later completion failure escape\n\nThe reattachment rewrite changes error selection: a later completion rejection can replace the original accepted-close error. ",
      "href": "#decision-failures",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "08\nUNEXPLAINED\nLeave fetch failure as a terminal path\n\nThe numeric resume check sits on the original execute socket. A failed result-fetch still goes to fail; increasing the field ",
      "href": "#decision-fetches",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "09\nSTATED\nMove compatibility knobs into tests\n\nSeven new test helpers translate legacy options into policies; a logger adapter is local to its test. Existing tests and benchmarks s",
      "href": "#decision-adapters",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "10\nUNEXPLAINED\nChange test inputs and recorded data\n\nTiny-limit normalization removes spilled-file evidence from some single-chunk cleanup tests. Helpers create output directories,",
      "href": "#decision-fixtures",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "11\nUNEXPLAINED\nRetire the local derivation suite and unused knob\n\nThe app’s memory derivation suite, including its literal 250 ms assertion, is deleted; related package tests alrea",
      "href": "#decision-tests",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "12\nUNEXPLAINED\nEnforce retired names with a source scan\n\nThe meta-test expands a production-source blacklist of retired constants, option names and the duplicate policy class. This",
      "href": "#decision-guards",
      "type": null,
      "visible": true
    },
